WEBVTT

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.960
"AUGUST 8, 2095"

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.130
"AUGUST 8, 2095"

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.130
Day Six of the Nine Schools Competition!

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:16.430
Today, the Battle Board and Ice
Pillars Break Rookie Events will be held!

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:30.280
Eimi! Good luck!

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.490
If I win here,
I'll be through to the finals!

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.990
Miyuki and Shizuku are already there!

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:39.160
I have to give it my best shot!

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.500
Whoever strikes first wins! Go!

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.230
I see.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:34.070
Because she's altered the phenomena
by moving her pillar,

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.900
it's impervious
to any changes from my magic.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.280
I already knew
you'd try an attack like that!

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.830
Nice going, Eimi!

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.750
Just keep going and lock up the win!

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:52.960
It's still too early to tell.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.500
Huh?

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:59.220
You're right. Surely, Third High
must've researched Eimi's strategy.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.010
Here's my next move!

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.030
All according to my calculations.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:21.110
That's our Shiori!

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:24.620
Yes. She certainly kept pace
with her opponent.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.990
What... What just happened?

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:30.500
Those pillars should've fallen over...

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.250
but they just kept sliding away!

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.000
I see. Pretty brilliant.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.250
Who would've thought she'd reduce
the ice's coefficient of friction to zero?

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.630
All right!

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.260
Right before the collision
with the opponent's pillar,

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.720
she minimizes the coefficient
of friction of her own pillar.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.720
The instant the three pillars become one,

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.270
she increases the coefficient
of friction to the max.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:54.850
The only one who can
pull off this move is Kanou,

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:57.650
a magician adept at detailed calculations.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:00.610
By now, Ms. Akechi is out of options.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:03.110
I'm going to take care of
her now in one fell swoop!

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.250
Airi...

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.420
I felt trapped by my family's issues
and tormented by my inferiority complex,

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.840
but it was you who taught me.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:24.010
There was something more important
that I could trust.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.430
I'm not going to look back anymore.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:30.430
I'm only going to look ahead
and not hold back. Just watch me.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:31.520
Airi!

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.320
Wh-What should I do?

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.070
Amelia? Amelia?

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:49.830
Amelia, listen closely...

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.460
Why now at a time like this?

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:55.790
"EIMI AKECHI (FIRST HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:02.420
"EIMI AKECHI (FIRST HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:02.420
Come to think of it, what was it
that Grandma said that day?

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.420
Come to think of it, what was it
that Grandma said that day?

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:09.050
It looks like I overestimated
First High's engineer.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:12.270
Oh no! It's over!

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:13.890
Not yet.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:18.060
There's no way that my brother
doesn't have a counterattack in mind.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.780
Well, we have no chance
against them in terms of control.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.440
Still, Eimi...

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:27.240
that's not your specialty, is it?

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.910
Is this going to end with me losing?

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:34.040
But I've worked hard to make it here.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.330
So everyone will forgive me, right?

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.290
I...

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:47.680
No...

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.510
I...

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.260
Look at Eimi's Psions!

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:54.810
I'm not...

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:56.180
going to...

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.850
stand for that!

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:09.700
No way! She's not capable
of an advanced move like that!

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.250
What...

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.910
did I just do?

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.170
Amelia...

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.750
That's right. With Magic Sumo.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.010
Yeah.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.880
I came really, really close...

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:28.510
but I lost!

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:32.800
Amelia, listen closely.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.350
You mustn't lie.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.390
Huh?

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:39.850
Magicians like you and me
turn lies into reality.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:43.650
That's why we must be careful about lying.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:48.530
Without our knowing it,
a lie can rewrite reality and become the truth.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.820
U-Um... Uh...

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:54.030
I suppose that's still
a little too hard for you.

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.830
One day you'll come to understand.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.790
One day...

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:04.130
Grandma, I get it now.

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.760
The truth is, I want to win!

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.510
I don't want to lose!

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:12.300
So, I'm going to do all I can
as far as I can go!

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.020
She did it!

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:25.440
Really, Eimi, who knew
you had all that hidden power?

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.400
But come to think of it...

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:32.070
Those card games
we've been playing every night...

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:36.910
Have you noticed that Eimi seems to
be losing just as much as she's winning?

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:38.160
Now that you mention it...

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.040
No way! That was on purpose?

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.370
Well, I can't say for sure.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:46.250
If Eimi has a habit of letting up
without knowing it,

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:49.090
but now she's unrestrained...

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:54.510
then this might be Eimi's true power.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:59.560
Who would've thought she was this powerful?
But most likely, Ms. Akechi, you're...

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:03.020
Three pillars versus two now!
This should do it!

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:06.360
Huh?

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:10.280
This is bad! It's sooner than we thought!

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:13.280
I knew your stamina
wouldn't hold up forever.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:18.030
I haven't lost yet!

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.910
I don't want to lose!

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:25.830
The only way to win is to hurl a pillar and
bring down her opponents' three remaining ones.

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:27.840
But even if she did manage to fling it,

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.800
those three are fused together
as a single unit now.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:35.840
Smashing into it to knock it over
will be nearly impossible.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:41.730
Now, it's only a matter of how
she'll bend reality with her magical power.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:46.560
For a magician, images are reality.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:48.940
Isn't that right, Grandma?

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:55.700
That's why I imagined myself smashing
my opponent's pillars over and over!

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.910
Please, let me deliver it!

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:02.330
All of my power in my final blow!

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.000
Go!

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:10.630
She still has that much power left?

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.010
I won't go down in defeat!

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:21.930
I'm focusing all of my Psions on defense!

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.200
No good, huh?

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.700
No! Hold up!

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:57.340
Well played.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.590
An utter defeat.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:11.820
Yippee ki yay!

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:15.860
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:16.530
"FINAL"
"EIMI AKECHI (FIRST HIGH)"
"SHIZUKU KITAYAMA (FIRST HIGH)"
"MIYUKI SHIBA (FIRST HIGH)"

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:20.240
Honoka, congratulations on making it
to the Battle Board final!

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.620
Congratulations to you and Shizuku, too!

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:28.790
This is amazing! I mean,
First High's swept all three spots in the final!

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:31.920
You guys...

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.800
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:36.720
Eimi!

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.260
D-Don't overdo it!

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:40.430
You should be in bed.

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:42.850
I-I'm fine, okay?

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.470
Ladies!

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:50.850
The Tournament Committee
has approached us with a proposal.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.520
Proposal?

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:58.860
First High has swept all three spots in the
Women's Ice Pillars Break Rookie Event final.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:00.820
So, they want to know

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:06.240
if we'd like to skip this afternoon's final
and have all three of you share first place.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:12.330
U-U-Um, I was thinking of withdrawing anyway
before you mentioned this proposal.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:14.170
Well, I guess I don't blame you!

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:18.300
This is awesome!
All three of you in first place!

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:21.050
Congratulations, all of you!

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:24.890
All right, then, we'll accept the proposal,
and you'll all take first place.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:26.260
Hold on a second.

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:32.770
I'd like to compete against Miyuki.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:50.290
Shizuku...

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:53.000
You heard Kitayama.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.790
What do you want to do, Miyuki?

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.420
I...

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:07.970
If Shizuku wishes to compete against me,
then I have no reason to refuse.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:10.770
I see.

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:14.270
In that case, I'll let
the Tournament Committee know.

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:15.650
Right!

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:25.700
"YAKISOBA"   "OKONOMIYAKI"

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:29.740
I didn't see that coming.
You going up against Miyuki.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:32.210
I guess that's how strongly
you felt about it, huh?

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:33.540
Yeah.

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:38.040
Because it's my chance.
I just didn't want to pass it up.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.210
Enrolling at First High...

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:42.090
and meeting Miyuki...

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:47.010
It shattered my ego to see someone
in my own class who's that amazing.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:50.180
The chance to go up against
a magician of Miyuki's caliber

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.020
doesn't come your way that often.

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.730
That's why I couldn't back down.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:13:00.940
I'm going to do everything I possibly can
in this match. No holding back.

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:02.900
Shizuku...

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:10.160
All right! Then, I'm rooting for you, Shizuku!
Give it all you've got!

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:14.620
I'm in the Battle Board final,
and you're in the Pillars Break final!

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:18.040
Let's both win our events
and celebrate together!

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:22.260
We're going to stuff ourselves
with the yummiest food and party all night!

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.800
I like it. Sounds fun.

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:27.010
Okay, let's promise each other!

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:28.680
We're both going to win!

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:31.100
Right. That's a promise.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:44.440
Airi...

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:46.650
I'm sorry I couldn't win.

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:48.910
It's all right. Don't worry about it.

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:51.160
It was such a good match.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:57.000
Thank you. I know I should feel bitter,
but somehow I feel so reinvigorated.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.540
I've never felt this way before.

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:02.670
Shiori, you've gotten stronger, I see.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:04.300
Even though I did lose.

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:07.300
But it's all thanks to you, Airi.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.390
What?

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:12.260
It's because of you that I learned
not to be shackled by my past

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:15.890
and to look straight ahead
toward the future.

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:17.310
Thanks.

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:32.370
Shizuku's amazing.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:36.450
I was so intimidated when I saw Miyuki.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.500
I have to do my best, too!

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:41.710
Yes, that's right!
You have to do your best!

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:43.710
Here we are in the finals.

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:47.470
I've been looking forward
to going one-on-one with you!

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:51.970
I'm sure you have some eye-popping tricks
up your sleeve for this match, too, yes?

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:55.600
I got a chance to see your Spirit Magic!

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:57.560
I'm not going to lose to you!

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.190
I'm going to beat you, no matter what!

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.440
Oh?

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:03.150
Well then, it's going to be
one fun match.

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:07.900
All right, I'll see you in the final!

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.740
Later!

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:15.040
I'm not used to doing that kind of thing.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:18.080
Is this Shizuku's influence?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:24.540
Mitsui, it seems like Tatsuya can't be spared
from Ice Pillars Break, after all.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.550
Well, it can't be helped, I guess.

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:30.090
After all, Tatsuya's in charge
of both Miyuki and Shizuku.

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:32.970
Oh, but I have a message from him.

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.010
What?

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:37.640
"If you stick to the plan
we came up with together, you can win it all.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:41.190
If the going gets tough,
then remember your training."

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.230
That's what he said!

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:44.730
Tatsuya...

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:50.990
So, your opponent in the final
is Third High's Tsukushiin, huh?

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:54.450
Spirit Magic that can manipulate
the water's surface.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:56.240
Do I have a chance?

00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:03.040
When she uses Spirit Magic, her Phenomena
Interference Power emits electromagnetic noise.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:05.130
Your chance of winning...

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:09.210
lies in that noise, Honoka.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.930
Understood! I'm heading over now!

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:25.440
And now, the Women's Battle Board
Rookie Event is about to start!

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:34.160
Mirroring Magic!

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:37.530
Since she's altering
the water's surface with magic,

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:41.330
it also has the effect
of blocking other spells.

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:44.500
So, it's like Area Interference.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:46.460
I managed to strike first!

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:50.510
Since Ancient Magic takes longer
to activate than Modern Magic!

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:54.510
Huh! I already took the flaws
of Ancient Magic into consideration.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:57.260
I'm abandoning
the first part of the race...

00:16:57.260 --> 00:16:59.350
to focus on the remainder!

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:09.440
I've seen this move before!

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:12.490
Is she planning to leap
over my magic range?

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:17.490
It's against the rules
to take a shortcut by using a Jump Spell!

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:18.870
All right!

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:22.370
I see! So she's jumping horizontally!

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:24.710
That wouldn't be a violation.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:29.670
But that's not the only thing I've got planned!

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:36.090
Honoka, your sensitivity to light
is your asset, right?

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:41.680
If you maximize that feature, you should
be able to sense Ms. Tsukushiin's noise.

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:44.140
That's your strength, Honoka.

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:46.850
I can see it now, Tatsuya!

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:50.190
Right where that light's shining...
That's where she's laid magic traps!

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:53.610
If I know where they are...

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:56.280
My spirits got suppressed?

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:59.740
That girl... Could it be
that she's the same as me?

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:01.990
Honoka Mitsui...

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:03.540
Mitsui...

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.210
I see!

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.460
So, that girl is a Light Element!

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.380
So, that's why she could see
my magic, huh?

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:13.550
No wonder I thought I could sense
something familiar about her!

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:19.550
This is just perfect!

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:24.520
This Nine Schools Competition
sure is a blast!

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:28.730
I can see the full course
from the top of this waterfall!

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:34.900
This is my chance to see all the spots
where she cast her magic!

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:37.570
What? Th-This many?

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:38.860
What should I do?

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:42.580
If I suppress them all,
it'll drain all my stamina!

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.250
I-I'll just start with the spots nearby!

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:47.910
What?

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:49.580
This feeling...

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:54.170
A dummy?

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:55.510
I knew it!

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:58.800
She realized that I could see
where she'd cast her magic,

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:01.760
and she used that dummy
to drain my power!

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:05.560
Well, sorry, but I'm not falling for that!

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:10.440
What?

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:13.360
What?

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:20.700
So, it wasn't just a dummy!
She actually unleashed something that huge, too?

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.490
Eat my dust!

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:24.120
Mitsui!

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:29.540
It's not over yet!
This match has only just begun!

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:34.090
What? That was a CAD, too?

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:38.380
That's not Ancient Magic!

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:40.590
That's Modern Magic!

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:46.350
Water Spirit?

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:49.890
Ancient Magic spells
are like my arms and legs.

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:52.100
I can use them in my sleep.

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:56.400
That's why I can focus on Modern Magic.

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:58.940
No good. I can't catch up!

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:05.700
Mitsui, try to remember
all that training you did

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:10.620
and all of the advice
that Tatsuya gave you!

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:19.010
Honoka...

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.420
What's going on?

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:23.890
That's right. I've trained
like there was no tomorrow!

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:26.720
I've worked hard along with everyone else!

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:31.560
Not to mention,
I've got Tatsuya on my side!

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.690
Suddenly, she's moving much better.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:37.230
We Elements have been known to unleash
powers that we didn't know we had,

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:43.490
for the sake of those we depend on.
Is that what this is?

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:45.530
Right, here's my killer move!

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.910
No matter what kind of wave
comes my way, I'm not going to lose!

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:59.590
I've caught up!

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:01.800
The race will come down
to that curve at the loop exit!

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:05.220
I've grabbed the inside track! I win!

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:06.390
What the...

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:07.640
How did that happen?

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:09.930
I had the inside track!

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:11.520
Illusion Magic!

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:14.060
She made her shadow darker
to create an optical illusion!

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:16.480
How did I miss that?

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:20.940
Tatsuya, the strategy you taught me
was a huge success!

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:23.570
Tatsuya!

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:25.160
I...

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:26.820
was able to win!

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:34.580
Oh man, she sure got me!

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:39.750
Who knew that I would suffer
an embarrassing defeat in a water sport?

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:44.090
I guess that goes to show
how strong your feelings were!

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:45.760
F-F-Feelings?

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:47.800
Toko...

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:51.180
Oh! I can't stand this!

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:53.060
Here, here.

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:57.520
--I won! I fought tooth and nail!
--I can't stand this!

00:21:57.520 --> 00:21:59.360
What about Shizuku?

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:06.450
Congratulations, Honoka.

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:08.910
Now, it's my turn.

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:47.010
"NEXT EPISODE"
